From 30ccdade0067bf2a7613b99c1d65cfeddf0b86a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CnsMaple <czy797@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:58:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(refined): add VSCode-based refined word-diff engine

Add a --word-diff-engine option (delta | refined, default delta). The "refined"
engine infers intra-line changes by treating each hunk's deletion run against its
addition run as one character-level change block, based on VSCode's
DefaultLinesDiffComputer (ported in src/refined_diff.rs): DP/LCS + Myers plus the
optimize/extend/remove-short/remove-very-short refine chain, with precise-mode
tweaks.

Behaviour:
- empty-change bars render as one-cell placeholders (braille blank) coloured by
  the opposite side: a minus-side bar = green (an addition), a plus-side bar = red
  (a deletion). Syntax highlighting runs on widened lines to keep delta's
  per-character superimpose invariant.
- the "\ No newline at end of file" marker is transparent, so a deletion run pairs
  with the following addition run instead of splitting into whole lines.
- short common runs are kept (remove_short_matches gap <= 1) and whitespace /
  indentation changes are marked; incidental space<->space reflow noise is dropped.
- a reflow junction placeholder marks where a split/joined line's content
  continues, only when the extra lines are a reflow (not a genuinely new line).

Selectable via CLI, git config delta.word-diff-engine, and reported by
--show-config. The default Levenshtein path is unchanged.

Also add a fork-only .github/workflows/release.yml (multi-platform build + GitHub
Release assets, without the upstream cargo/winget publish jobs).
